subproblem.statement:
Let P, n ∈ ℕ and let c : ℝ → ℝⁿ → ℝ^{n+1} satisfy c(s,w)_0 = s and c(s,w)_{i+1} = w_i. Assume:
- ψ : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ^P is C¹, V ⊆ ℝ^{n+1}, ψ is injective on V and Dψ(y) is injective for y ∈ V;
- F : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ is C¹;
- Ω ⊆ ℝ^{n+1} is open, and Θ : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ^{n+1} is C¹ on Ω and injective on Ω, with DΘ(z) injective for z ∈ Ω, Θ(Ω) ⊆ V and F(Θ(z)) = z_0 for z ∈ Ω.
Fix t ∈ ℝ, and let Ω^t := {w ∈ ℝⁿ : c(t,w) ∈ Ω} and χ(w) := ψ(Θ(c(t,w))). Then Ω^t is open and χ is C¹ and injective on Ω^t. Moreover, for every w ∈ Ω^t, with z := c(t,w) and y := Θ(z):
- DF(y) ≠ 0 and Dχ(w) is injective;
- for every v ∈ Dψ(y)(ℝ^{n+1}) with ⟨v, Dψ(y)e⟩ = DF(y)e for all e, Dχ(w)(ℝⁿ) = Dψ(y)(ℝ^{n+1}) ∩ (ℝv)^⊥ and √det(Dχ(w)*Dχ(w)) = |v|·√det(Dψ(y)*Dψ(y))·|det DΘ(z)|.
